# Story 17: Closing & Renaming Panes (40s)
# Hook: Keep your workspace tidy: close panes you're done with and name the ones you keep.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-017-closing-renaming-panes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Keep your workspace tidy: close panes you're done with and name the ones you keep.

[00:04.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and split into a couple of panes to work with.

[00:09.0 --> 00:14.0]
Ctrl+P, n gives us a second pane.

[00:14.0 --> 00:22.0]
Press Ctrl+P then r to rename the active pane. Type the name and press Enter.

[00:22.0 --> 00:30.0]
You can also set the given-name from rysh mode. ##pane name keeps it unique per lane.

[00:30.0 --> 00:36.0]
When you're finished with a pane, Ctrl+P then x closes it.

[00:36.0 --> 00:40.0]
Rename to stay organized, close to clean up. Your layout, your rules.

